        "title": "fix: redact colon and folded bearer diagnostics",
        "body": "Closes #936.\n\nRedacts colon-delimited and line-folded bearer credentials in both the Go CLI and Worker diagnostic redaction paths. Adds regression coverage for the previously leaking encodings while preserving existing structured credential redaction.\n\nProof requested by ClawSweeper:\n\n```text\n$ go run .\ngo_header_colon output=\"Authorization: [redacted]\\nendpoint=https://api.example.invalid\" leaked=false\ngo_bearer_fold output=\"diagnostic Bearer [redacted] from provider\" leaked=false\n\n$ node /tmp/crabbox-proof-940/worker/worker-proof.mjs\nworker_header_colon output=\"Authorization: [redacted]\\nendpoint=https://worker.example.invalid\" leaked=false\nworker_bearer_fold output=\"diagnostic Bearer [redacted] from provider\" leaked=false\n```\n\nThe Go proof is a throwaway module under `/tmp/crabbox-proof-940/go` importing the real `github.com/openclaw/crabbox/internal/cli` helper from this branch. The Worker proof bundles a throwaway script that imports the real `worker/src/http.ts` redaction helper from this branch.\n",
